Makes an animated gif of the TimeWalkCleaning time walk on one event: the 8 PE seed stage (panel 2),
then the 4 PE extension stage (panel 3).
The camera is the same 2D histogram as the cleaning's panels and shows every pixel's PE at the time bin
of the frame. Each step of the walk is one pixel (the parent) searching its neighbours for signal in
its own time bin +/- 2. The gif steps through that window one time bin per frame, then a result frame
shows which neighbours joined. The last frame is the finished cluster at the triggered pixel's peak
bin, where the cleaning reads its images.

The walk is rerun here, not read back from the cleaning's output, so the settings at the top of
PlotTimeWalkGif.h are copied from event_cleaning/TimeWalkCleaning/EventCleaning.h. If one changes
there, change it here too.

How to remake the executable
>./compile_script.sh
(or ./compile_script.sh clean first; the Makefile does not track the header, so after editing
PlotTimeWalkGif.h run rm PlotTimeWalkGif.o first)

How to run
>./run_script.sh /DataAnalysis/MakeThingsPretty/TimeWalkGiFs/TimeWalkGifs.txt

RISE_FRACTION=<percent> and TIME_WINDOW=<n> work the same way as for the cleaning's run_script.sh:
>RISE_FRACTION=30 TIME_WINDOW=3 ./run_script.sh /DataAnalysis/MakeThingsPretty/TimeWalkGiFs/TimeWalkGifs.txt

gifs are created in ./Gifs as <Output>_E<event>_tw_<n>_rf_<percent>.gif


Gif list file, one row per event, no spaces:
Output,File,Event

- Output: name for the gif, the event number and settings are added to it
- File:   full path, either a merged data file or a sim _tdem.root file
    data: /cedar/DataAnalysis/MergedData/Output/<night>/Merged_....root
    sims: /cedar/simdata/sofiadata/20260827_taudavid/<run>/CARE/Tilt_90.000000/<shower>_tdem.root
- Event:  Test tree entry number (the E# of the cleaning PDF for data)


What the outlines mean
- white:   in the cluster from the 8 PE stage (T = triggered pixel, where the walk starts)
- magenta: in the cluster from the 4 PE stage
- orange:  the pixel searching its neighbours
- cyan:    a neighbour being searched, the number is its PE in the bin shown
- green:   a neighbour at or above the threshold in the bin shown (it joins)
- grey dashed (result frames): a neighbour that never reached the threshold in the window
On result frames the numbers are each neighbour's brightest PE anywhere in the window.

Settings in PlotTimeWalkGif.h
- ShowEveryWindowBin = false keeps only the result frames, for a shorter gif of a big event
- the frame delays (IntroFrameDelay, SweepFrameDelay, ...) are in centiseconds
- PrintWalkDiagnostics prints every admitted/rejected neighbour in the cleaning's own format

Calibration is the same as the cleaning (flasher x SiPM gain for data, 24.1 ADC per PE for sims).
2025 nights whose flasher file only has a CamFlasher histogram (e.g. 20250125) still make a gif, with
a WARNING: the cleaning itself stops on those nights (ExACT asks for CamFlasher44), so there is no
cleaning output to compare that walk with.
